; dd.lab.test: parent of the dns_depth zones. No CAA here: a child without its own CAA
; (nocaa) is covered by none (lab.test answers "no CAA" too, Corefile.res).
; labdns appends one DS record per signed child at lab start (keys are never committed).
$ORIGIN dd.lab.test.
$TTL 300
@        IN SOA ns.dns.lab.test. hostmaster.dns.lab.test. 1 7200 3600 1209600 300
@        IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
good        IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
broken      IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
unsigned    IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
nocaa       IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
nosts       IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
nomail      IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
ststesting  IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
stsbroken   IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
stsmismatch IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
notlsrpt    IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
dkim1024    IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
dkim512     IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
